    "nci_treatment": "No material non-controlling interests.",
    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF component DCF (routing table row 1: operating company, US tech hardware/software). First valuation of CSCO; no prior DCF and no memory entry. NET DEBT: total debt $29,533M (short-term debt $10,161M incl. $6.7B commercial paper + long-term debt $19,372M, per 10-K MD&A 'Total debt') less cash, cash equivalents and investments $14,297M = $15,236M. The CSV TotalDebt of $33,033M double-counts the $3.5B current portion of long-term debt (LongTermDebt 22,872 + DebtCurrent 10,161) and was not used. Non-marketable equity investments are excluded from the bridge (conservative). INTEREST INCOME: Cisco is net-debt, so interest income ($866M FY26) is not deducted from the owner-FCF base; the component build is unlevered and cash is credited once in the bridge. OWNER FCF FY26: reported FCF $12,767M - SBC incl. withholding $5,703M = $7,064M. This base is depressed by the final $2.3B US transition-tax (TCJA) payment in FY26 and a ~$2B working-capital build for AI/hyperscaler product shipments; normalised for the transition tax it is ~$9.4B, and on an unlevered basis (adding back ~$0.5B after-tax net interest) ~$9.9B (15.6% of revenue). The component build's year-1 owner-FCF margin (~19-20%) is above that because (i) the transition tax is gone, (ii) FY27 guidance implies ~1pp non-GAAP operating margin expansion, and (iii) year-1 revenue is +15%. SBC: withholding taxes on net-share settlement ($1,873M) are elevated by the ~60% share-price rise over FY26; the forward sbc_pct path starts at 8.3% (SBC ~5.6-6% + withholding ~2.5%) rather than the 9.0% FY26 print, declining 0.1-0.2pp/yr. BUYBACKS: Cisco is a repurchaser ($6.1B FY26, $8.1B authorisation remaining) plus ~$6.5B dividends; the flat share count is funded, not a modelling convention. EBITDA margin is pre-SBC but AFTER restructuring (~$0.7B/yr, recurring at Cisco for a decade), i.e. GAAP op income + D&A + SBC = 34.3% in FY26. D&A path reflects acquired-intangible amortisation rolling off (next-12-month amortisation $1,534M per 10-K). Cash tax: normalised FY26 cash tax ex transition tax ~$2.5B (~16% of GAAP pretax); FY27 guide 15% GAAP / 18.5% non-GAAP effective rate; model 17% ramping to 19%.",
